<h1 class="page-title">Hubworld</h1>
<p class="standfirst">Sound design &middot; 2024 &middot; a short film by Bitcrush</p>

<p>Hubworld is an animated short by Chris Erickson (Bitcrush). A faceless character wanders through an old virtual world on the day it shuts down: a calm, slightly wistful journey rather than a story with big turns. Oli Leverton wrote the score, and I did the sound design.</p>

{% video { youtube: "o6zwMPDenAY", title: "Hubworld, a short film", caption: "Hubworld, with Oli Leverton's score and my sound design." } %}

<h2>Sound</h2>
<p>Almost all of it happens inside a virtual world, so I wanted the sound to feel a little fake, like an old web game: low sample rates and bit depths, and the same samples repeated on purpose. I made many of the effects from scratch in BFXR, a tiny retro sound-effect synth (the footsteps, birds, pickups and the orb), and its limits were the point: they're the ones old game sound designers worked within. The welcome character speaks in an AI voice, to set this world apart from the real one.</p>
<p>The old chrome giant needed to feel ancient and falling apart, so it moves to the creak of a train track, recorded with a contact mic and layered for weight. I also let each new place in a little early: the seagulls start a moment before we cut to the beach, and the crows before the plains, so the scenes flow into each other.</p>

